        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c6160d89-dcea-3640-b7ed-e8ab044464ee",
                "word": "prédilection",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9313bab3-ef09-45cb-baff-e6e3f8ea805d",
                        "entry_id": "c6160d89-dcea-3640-b7ed-e8ab044464ee",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "prédilections"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                        "entry_id": "c6160d89-dcea-3640-b7ed-e8ab044464ee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Préférence d’amitié, d’affection, de goût."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35f88df1-fc17-45d8-8d92-423c1f0ecf32",
                                "sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                                "text": "Je devine toujours la raison de ces prédilections que dans le monde on qualifie poliment d'indéfinissables !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d8004bc-3c82-4b33-9a53-1a1b7e3b3d03",
                                "sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                                "text": "Comme je n'avais aucune prédilection particulière pour la mer de glace, je remis au lendemain la visite que je comptais lui faire, et nous partîmes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "302893fe-9bdb-4992-8801-4cef3ed5289c",
                                "sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                                "text": "Depuis longtemps, l'église était devenue froide et, sauf le dimanche, on n'y rencontrait plus guère, en dehors des offices, de ces fidèles furtifs qui aiment à confier en passant une petite prière à leur saint de prédilection."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50e80af4-685a-44ab-b71a-d529ed4de4bf",
                                "sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                                "text": "Chaque tendeur paraît avoir une essence de prédilection pour ses hayettes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bd0ae36-0442-4ef7-b4f8-0a2e07cef28d",
                                "sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                                "text": "Bol (22 ans), médaillée de bronze olympique du 400 m haies l’été dernier et récente vice-championne du monde de la spécialité, s’est imposée en 52 sec 67 dans sa course de prédilection, largement devant deux Ukrainiennes Viktoriya Tkachuk (54.30) et Anna Ryzhykova (54.86)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b4eba0f-eab8-42fc-9a3e-549328f5f25b",
                                "sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                                "text": "Bien acagnardé contre le zinc à pampres de son estaminet de prédilection, Antonin lantiponait à foison parmi des norias de pieds nickelés en mouillage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dffd5043-25a6-45f0-95f7-8ddecacc3049",
                                "sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                                "text": "Ali Assani, un Comorien surnommé Kaf’Bob en hommage à Bob Marley, mais surtout à cause de sa tignasse poussiéreuse de Rasta, et de son goût immodéré pour le reggae et le zamal – pas forcément dans cet ordre de prédilection, d’ailleurs – complétait le trio."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "57c99306-e38b-4b09-9f09-391784b7e2aa",
                        "source_entry_id": "c6160d89-dcea-3640-b7ed-e8ab044464ee",
                        "source_sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
                        "target_lang_word": "predilection",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "predilection",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                        "entry_id": "b330d9e8-bfe3-3108-99e5-1906471a0108",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A condition of favoring or liking; a tendency towards; proclivity; predisposition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfb69b06-e5c2-45ff-91f4-8c5d3f2c4625",
                                                "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                                "text": "The young King looked tenderly at Mademoiselle Mancini, who gave him a glance quite as tender in return—not, however, unobserved. His mother had been for some time past a displeased spectator of a predilection which might become dangerous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9204ffc3-4c8c-4993-a588-288c09dc8f69",
                                                "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                                "text": "American operating practice aims at the minimum wastage of time by locomotives at water columns and coal stages, and this predilection for shunters with high capacity tenders is thereby explained."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4be4404f-7d65-41ff-b5f7-10c8e51e697e",
                                                "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                                "text": "It was an illusion, of course, generated by Clevinger's predilection for staring fixedly at one side of a question and never seeing the other side at all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28b624fb-1219-475b-ab2a-b814d6206610",
                                                "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                                "text": "The appointment as Member of the B.T.C. with \"special responsibility for railway workshops\" of Sir Steuart Mitchell is in accordance with Mr. Marples' predilection for non-railwaymen in the highest posts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "196236f5-8c72-4b4f-83a2-e93976ed539f",
                                                "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                                "text": "A row of houses he regards as a row of necessary evils. The softening and degeneration of the human race he attributes to its progressive predilection for interiors and waning interest in the art of going out and staying there."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2942dc55-6d24-4b45-b813-792ce084d33c",
                                                "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                                "text": "But for him the first rule of judging was to set aside personal predilection and vote the law and the facts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af1ed5df-ce89-45c7-b2fd-74279516e48e",
                                                "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                                "text": "... youth’s predilection for revolt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dadaa914-f401-4d4b-81f5-b1630833edd4",
                                                "sense_id": "7e515239-afa6-38aa-b6fa-ec58c1646d55",
                                                "text": "Wilson doesn’t see any inconsistency between his socialism and his predilection for the high life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7d797894-0b62-4f03-89bd-f8b2b7d2caa5",
                        "source_entry_id": "c6160d89-dcea-3640-b7ed-e8ab044464ee",
                        "source_sense_id": "4443d87f-1253-3fe0-afb3-0f8d41e07962",
